To avoid parking a reviewed, green PR on a recommendation-engine outage, I dispatched close-out directly with a written prompt: `POST /dispatch`, item `66048f8e`. Direct dispatch does not call OpenRouter.

It keeps every gate:
- CI concluded on the head;
- each `4da8ceef` condition verified;
- the `bb504906` security condition checked in code, with a do-not-merge stop if it fails;
- merge, then `ci-success` on the merge commit;
- LIN-3135 left open for the Simple Dispatcher `mintBrokerToken` `{itemId}` change.

This is an engineering routing call, not a security one. The steps of the merge gate are unchanged.

